WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.360
When you make a cartoon about a prehistoric
family, you usually end up taking a few liberties

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.570
with reality.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:11.589
From caveman strength to Paleolithic physics,
here are some things that only adults notice

00:00:11.589 --> 00:00:12.679
in The Croods.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:16.700
The environment the Croods reside in is stark
and barren.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:21.830
It's a dusty wasteland occupied by feisty
birds and a cat-owl hybrid with a caveman

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:22.830
vendetta.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.339
Don't sweat it though, kiddos, our ancestors
are mighty and resilient.

00:00:26.339 --> 00:00:29.140
They can throw massive stones and run like
the wind.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.210
It's a cartoon grab bag of Wile E. Coyote
shenanigans.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:36.750
However, in the first few minutes — after
an outstretched hall-of-fame catch sends him

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:41.790
sliding headfirst into a boulder — the family's
patriarch, Grug, throws out a light-hearted

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:45.330
quip that will have parents raising an eyebrow
or two.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:50.270
After fighting tooth and nail for their breakfast,
which is just one big egg, Grug ends up only

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.469
getting a smidgeon of a portion by the time
the family has had their fill.

00:00:54.469 --> 00:00:55.469
His response?

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:56.469
"Oh, that's all right.

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:57.859
I ate last week."

00:00:57.859 --> 00:01:00.870
Contextually, the joke works and sets a fun
tone.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.970
But given all their physical advantages, it's
surprising that the Croods are able to maintain

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:08.229
their hulkish physiques eating only one egg
per week.

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:12.560
They need to eat in order to survive, and
that's made clear throughout the journey.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.610
Maybe it's the caveman DNA, because once we
meet Guy, he's a bit leaner and not nearly

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.100
as strong as any of the Croods.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.720
That's an interesting fact given that he has
an easier time getting food and even introduces

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.330
them to the concept of "leftovers."

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.520
The leader of the pack is the steadfast father
figure, Grug, and he's done what every parent

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.740
hopes to achieve — he's kept his children
alive by instilling in them a perpetual fear

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:38.740
of everything.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.360
Granted, it comes from a nurturing place.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.920
Considering we believe them to be the last
caveman family — and every other family

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:49.240
around them has succumbed to the horrors of
their world — it's reasonable that he chooses

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.610
to lead this way.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:55.460
But is this almighty head of the family content
in his role as beefcake supreme?

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.710
Of course not.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.960
Any deviation from his plans causes him to
become frantic.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.820
He's so overbearing that his wife Ugga has
to physically put her hands on him and push

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.700
him away at one point.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.880
Good thing there's some modicum of modern
family roles in this Stone Age family, otherwise

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.940
this adventure could've gotten dark.

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.910
With their circumstances, there are unfortunate
attributes that need to be overlooked for

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:18.430
the sake of survival.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.870
Grug's incessant neediness is one of them.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.450
He needs his hand held through most of the
film.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.130
When it comes time to sink or swim, we watch
Grug sink to the bottom of a lake with all

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.120
the melancholy a primitive mind can muster.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.500
Kids will think Grug is being a goofball.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.230
Adults will empathize with his plight.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:37.810
And everyone will feel like he's smothering
them.

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.550
The human vocal range, unfortunately, has
its limits.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:45.800
We can only shout for so long, and our voices
can only reach so far.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.950
Good thing our ancestors wrapped their lips
around the husks of abandoned snail houses

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:52.660
and discovered the booming might of the conch.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.520
It would appear the ancient founder of the
first megaphone was none other than Guy.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:03:01.420
The conch shell is formed by aquatic snails
and is mostly found near large water sources.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:06.250
To find one anywhere but the ocean is extremely
rare and usually means that an ancient waterway

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.010
once existed there.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.120
And at the end of The Croods, our heroes all
reach the ocean and venture onward into the

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.940
next chapter of their story.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:18.170
The fact that this is their final destination
in the film implies everyone had yet to reach

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.620
the ocean before.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.770
So how is it they possess so many of these
conch shells?

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.620
Guy is handing them out like candy.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.310
Even the most inquisitive kid may be surprised
at the surplus of conch shells that Guy has

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.380
in his satchel when they're setting off into
a labyrinth of tunnels.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:37.590
Guy may be an idea man, but he still seems
naive enough to believe he can actually catch

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.590
the sun.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:42.440
Chances are he hadn't spent a lot of his time
alone out in a different ocean, farming for

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.440
conch shells.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:48.140
In the apparent final moments of Grug's time
with his family, he sums up everything that

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.300
he and his daughter Eep need to talk about
beautifully.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:55.810
It's the most succinct the moment could possibly
be, with the caveman pulling his daughter

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:56.860
in for a hug.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:04:00.350
She then inquires as to the name of this new
comforting invention.

00:04:00.350 --> 00:04:02.570
He declares that it will be called a hug

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.640
"Because it rhymes with Grug."

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.280
It's a misty-eyed moment that ends in a father
telling his daughter he loves her.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.860
The kids have probably checked out on the
mushy stuff at this point, but adults are

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.160
probably asking how the heck there's a word
for something as complex as "love" but not

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:18.700
something as straightforward as a "hug."

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:23.170
Cavemen are extremely literal, as displayed
by Eep's innocent assumption that fire is

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:25.950
alive because Guy said it was "dying."

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:31.120
The words they use are attached to actions
and things — caves, rocks, run, smash, etc.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.800
It's cute to have "hug" be introduced into
their lexicon — thus displaying Grug's contribution

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.390
and evolution — but anyone who's had their
heart put through the ringer knows "love"

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:42.910
is a drastically more complex word to process.

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:47.070
It feels like a missed opportunity to build
on the formula and bring in the Neanderthals'

00:04:47.070 --> 00:04:49.030
interpretation of the emotion.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:52.710
Maybe the film's creators felt like that would
be too much mushy stuff.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.200
Anyone trying not to cry in front of their
kids when the Croods all pay tribute to their

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:58.090
fallen patriarch will agree.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:03.230
It's unlikely that children are keying in
on metaphors when they're indulging in a visual

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:08.460
blitz of colors and silliness, but adults
may have a hard time not seeing cultural similarities

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:11.900
between our world and the caveman world running
through The Croods.

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:15.730
It's all the more obvious with Nicolas Cage
stepping in as the dad who won't change with

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:16.840
the times.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:21.980
His dry, annoyed drawl helps the movie drive
its point home — adapt or slip into a crack

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.300
in the ground and melt into a river of magma.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.390
There's another character whose visual attributes
also help make things apparent, and that's

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:30.390
Guy, of course.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:34.810
The scrawny idea factory's representation
of progress is visualized, with a healthy

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.320
dose of snark, by his man bun.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:42.170
The hairstyle is a telltale sign of the liberal
hipster, especially considering when the movie

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:44.420
was released, in 2013.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:49.200
Guy innocently posits a better approach to
situations they have long dealt with, but

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.990
he lacks the leadership that comes from years
of fighting off predators with your fists.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.990
And it's not that Grug or Guy are wrong about
their approaches — they're just different.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.210
If any parents are upset with the representation
of either side, then they're looking at the

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.240
entire film all wrong.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.200
After all, our heroes reach their new paradise
by working together.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:12.270
Each of them grows in their own way and learns
an unfortunate lesson in the process — mother-in-laws

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.980
are immortal, and you best just get used to
them.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:20.480
Anyone who's taken part in a Boy Scout camping
trip and felt a primal rage bubble up from

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.970
within while they spin sticks between kindling
might have some major issues with the way

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:26.860
The Croods deals with fire.

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:31.200
Trying to master the strike of flint is an
incredibly annoying endeavor, but evidently,

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:35.640
Guy doesn't have an issue sparking up some
flames in a heartbeat in the middle of stressful

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.640
situations.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.340
Heck, he can create a fire strong enough to
withstand the wind gusts of thousands of carnivorous

00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:42.340
birds.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.140
"It comes from where you come from?"

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.870
"No, I make it."

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.450
"Make some for me!"

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:51.740
Child audiences are no doubt unaware of the
woes of campfire construction, as camping

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:55.070
often means electrical outlets and parking
spaces nowadays.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:59.080
Those of us who endured the "joy" of camping
in the middle of nowhere know how difficult

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.140
the fire-building process can be.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:02.800
We'll let it slide, though.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:06.480
After all, it's more enjoyable to see how
things pan out for the Croods instead of them

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:09.180
getting mauled by the wave of flesh-eating
birds.

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:14.050
It also makes the family's introduction to
Guy and the concept of fire a majestic experience.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:19.990
The zany Looney Tunes tomfoolery of The Croods
injects the proper amount of innocence into

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:24.860
what might otherwise be a boring tale about
how even Nicolas Cage can change.

00:07:24.860 --> 00:07:28.480
However, the film begins to stretch it a bit
far at points.

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:32.490
It's a child's animated film, and we're trying
not to nitpick, but right around the time

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:37.720
Grug grabs the family and leaps off a cliff,
most adults are spitting out their chardonnay,

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:42.740
completely flabbergasted that they all could
survive a fall from the equivalent of a skyscraper

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:43.740
rooftop.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:46.960
Well, it's a good thing that cavemen are immune
to falls, apparently.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.000
Especially Gran, who can take quite a beating
for an elderly woman in need of a walking

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.000
cane.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.570
The first time we see the family hunt, the
roles are decided by Gran being substituted

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:59.610
for a quarter, and she's tossed into the air
in a game of heads or tails.

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:04.639
In any animated adventure, a few falls are
expected, and they induce the necessary giggles.

00:08:04.639 --> 00:08:07.180
But The Croods stretches it to the point of
incredulity.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.410
They fall a lot.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:13.100
The family members are launched into the sky
by a whale geyser and land on their faces

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.100
in a field.

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:18.110
They fall into giant mazes after the ground
decides to suddenly explode.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:21.910
They even get slingshotted into the air by
trap mishaps.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:25.800
But every time they fall, they just get right
back up, which is actually kind of a sweet

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:26.870
message for kids.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.520
In the real world, it takes much longer than
we'd like to teach a cute little puppy that

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.120
the rug is not an appropriate place to drop
off a fresh loaf.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.860
In other words, adults are all too aware of
nature's primal indifference.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:42.750
Kids are spoiled by generations of species'
taming and most likely haven't been kicked

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.110
by a mule while trying to get fresh milk for
their Fruity Pebbles.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:50.260
So, when the Croods amass a healthy collection
of pet friends by the end of their journey,

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.700
the little ones don't even bat an eyelash.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:57.040
According to our favorite cave-dwelling family
unit, animals are shockingly easy to tame

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.730
in the Paleolithic era.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:03.230
The Croods even gain a mount in the form of
a different version of the hellish owl-cat

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.670
that was hunting them at the beginning of
the film.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:08.570
But there's no explanation as to how they
tame that beast.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:12.200
The implication is that animals come with
a built in "pet" setting.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:16.190
The only thing you need to do in order to
flip that switch is to not run away screaming.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:21.300
When the walls of the Croods' little ravine
suddenly come smashing together, they lose

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:24.180
their cave — the only safe hideaway they've
ever known.

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:28.960
To the amazement of the family, though, just
behind their cave walls is a vibrant jungle.

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.670
All it took was tectonic calamity to expose
them to a world that looks suspiciously like

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.080
James Cameron's Avatar.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:39.790
Obviously, they aren't actually on the mystical
moon of Pandora, but the environment is lush

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:44.710
and colorful enough to make you think that
a rich vein of unobtanium runs beneath the

00:09:44.710 --> 00:09:45.710
surface.

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.650
Not to say animators took a page from the
Cameron Bible, but the vivid colors all breathe

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.090
a certain familiarity into the jungle.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:56.280
Kids respond to bright, colorful images, so
we can't claim the market has been cornered

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.600
on the color spectrum.

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.839
But the creatures we come across don't help
differentiate from the two worlds, like the

00:10:01.839 --> 00:10:06.090
flock of dual-winged birds flying over the
beach in the final sequences.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:10.830
Giant rideable tigers and vibrant, sentient
flowers also help The Croods' world feel reminiscent

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.020
of Pandora.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:16.210
Most likely, it's just us jaded adults being
unable to enjoy new things and connecting

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:17.730
with Grug too much.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:20.100
After all, no one's got a monopoly on pretty
colors.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:25.000
Still, if you squint, it's a little hard to
tell the difference between the two films.

